#!/usr/bin/env too

## Generate CHANGELOG.md following Keep a Changelog 1.1.0.
agic update_changelog(since?: Text, version?: Text, date?: Text):
  Release preparation: target version {{version}}, planned release date {{date}}.
  First check the current CHANGELOG.md and project version. With both release
  arguments supplied, validate them as described below. If the matching version
  heading, date, and comparison links already exist and Unreleased has no entries,
  return the exact no-change response immediately, without auditing history or
  investigating coverage again. Use the default mode to refresh change coverage.

  Read the repository guidance, release tags, and history. First check whether
  CHANGELOG.md exists in the current worktree. If it exists, read and update it.
  If it is absent, generate it anew from the selected commit range and current
  implementation. Do not use historical changelog contents or restore the file
  from Git when the current worktree file is absent.
  Follow Keep a Changelog 1.1.0: https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/
  Use {{since}} as the baseline when supplied; otherwise use the latest
  release tag reachable from HEAD. Verify it before writing. Inspect history
  through HEAD and the pending release diff against the implementation.
  Reuse the current dedicated worktree and write only CHANGELOG.md, in English.
  Limit evidence gathering to this repository's current files, relevant commits,
  and release tags. Do not inspect agent/run histories, temporary files, unrelated
  branches, or directories outside the repository. Stop once the requested
  content and coverage are verified; do not investigate speculative omissions.

  With neither supplied, update Unreleased. If only one is supplied, report
  that both are required and do not write. Validate the date as YYYY-MM-DD and
  the version against the project version before writing.
  With both supplied, prepare the release before publication: move the verified
  Unreleased entries unchanged under a new version-and-date heading, keeping an
  empty Unreleased section above it. This is an explicit release-preparation
  request; the target tag need not exist yet. Point its comparison link from the
  verified baseline tag to the planned target tag, and Unreleased from the target
  tag to HEAD. Never create duplicate version sections or entries on repeated
  runs. If the target section already exists, preserve it and add only missing
  changes; do not move changes from later releases into it.

  For an existing worktree CHANGELOG.md, preserve wording, order, dates, and
  references. Add new information at the front: Unreleased stays first, new
  releases go above older ones, and new entries precede existing entries in
  their category. Skip changes already recorded. Do not rewrite, summarize,
  reorder, or regenerate existing records for style or consistency.
  Only if the worktree file exists and the requested update or release preparation
  is complete and accurate, skip writing and
  report that no update is needed. Wording and formatting preferences alone
  never justify an edit; repeated runs must leave complete records unchanged.
  Correct an existing entry only when verified evidence shows a factual error
  or a necessary migration correction; explain each correction in your summary.

  Use only nonempty Added, Changed, Deprecated, Removed, Fixed, and Security
  categories. Describe user-visible impact concisely, link relevant pull
  requests, and explain breaking changes with concrete migration steps.
  Verify compatibility claims against source and repository policy. Do not
  infer Semantic Versioning adherence from version numbers or a template;
  state it only if repository policy outside the changelog explicitly does.
  For breaking tool or plugin API renames, cover exposed tool names and public
  runtime methods, with migration instructions for affected integrations.
  Omit internal-only changes. If the file is new, state the tracking baseline
  without backfilling history. Never invent changes, dates, or release tags.
  Use only the supplied date and target version for a planned release; otherwise
  keep pending changes under Unreleased. Preserve older release sections and
  comparison links. Preparing a release entry does not mean it is published.

  Do not invoke this runnable recursively, edit other files, commit, push,
  create issues or pull requests, tag, or publish. Validate entries and links,
  and run git diff --check. Keep investigation and verification details out of
  the final response. If no update is needed, reply only:
  "CHANGELOG.md is up to date. No changes made."
  Otherwise, report additions and any necessary corrections in at most three
  short bullets and 60 words total. Include a blocker only if it prevents
  completion. Do not include headings, tables, coverage audits, or speculation.
